  "clips": [
    {
      "key": "clerk-2a3f913d43bd10c3",
      "character": "clerk",
      "speaker": "Clerk",
      "text": "After some funerals you'll prepare the body yourself, and there'll be a choice. A ring left on a finger. A fat wallet. Take it, or leave it. That's karma. Be good and the town trusts you: calmer, richer customers. Be bad and the money's nice, the hours are flexible, and the Guild pretends it doesn't know you.",
      "part": "whole",
      "rulesets": [
        "expanded"
      ],
      "file": {
        "ogg": "clerk/clerk-2a3f913d43bd10c3.ogg",
        "m4a": "clerk/clerk-2a3f913d43bd10c3.m4a",
        "bytes": 202666
      },
      "duration": 21.57
    },
    {
      "key": "clerk-240963811aec56a7",
      "character": "clerk",
      "speaker": "Clerk",
      "text": "Cash is for the business. Di-Mart sells caskets wholesale; ask for Elijah, and don't let him touch your hair. Selling from stock pays better than a rush order. Your office has upgrades: paint, a coffee machine, one day a chapel. That's it! Your first customer is waiting. I'll be watching. Taking notes. Don't mind me.",
      "part": "whole",
      "rulesets": [
        "expanded"
      ],
      "file": {
        "ogg": "clerk/clerk-240963811aec56a7.ogg",
        "m4a": "clerk/clerk-240963811aec56a7.m4a",
        "bytes": 185359
      },
      "duration": 19.77
    },
    {
      "key": "clerk-e321c7a9632dde83",
      "character": "clerk",
      "speaker": "Clerk",
      "text": "Every customer has a limit: the most they'll spend. You never see it. You see an estimate, a range, and the real number is somewhere inside it. Not necessarily the middle. Psychology classes at Spirit University narrow it down. Nothing you sell can push the bill past their limit. They'll just say no.",
      "part": "whole",
      "rulesets": [
        "expanded"
      ],
      "file": {
        "ogg": "clerk/clerk-e321c7a9632dde83.ogg",
        "m4a": "clerk/clerk-e321c7a9632dde83.m4a",
        "bytes": 178231
      },
      "duration": 18.73
    },
    {
      "key": "clerk-d5d0b470b26e0e76",
      "character": "clerk",
      "speaker": "Clerk",
      "text": "Every day you get turns. Each customer you meet costs one. Unused turns carry over to tomorrow, but only up to one day's worth, so sleeping in all week won't make you rich. Every funeral earns Bury Points. Whoever has the most at the end of the season wins, and gets to be smug at the Guild picnic.",
      "part": "whole",
      "rulesets": [
        "expanded"
      ],
      "file": {
        "ogg": "clerk/clerk-d5d0b470b26e0e76.ogg",
        "m4a": "clerk/clerk-d5d0b470b26e0e76.m4a",
        "bytes": 178894
      },
      "duration": 18.78
    },
    {
      "key": "clerk-0a7515bb2f88f861",
      "character": "clerk",
      "speaker": "Clerk",
      "text": "Here's the trick. Land the bill within 8% of their limit and you get a bonus. Within 3%, a bigger one. Hit it to the dollar and the whole town reads about it in the paper. Every price in this business is a multiple of fifty dollars, so the exact number can always be reached. In theory. In practice, people cry on the calculator.",
      "part": "whole",
      "rulesets": [
        "expanded"
      ],
      "file": {
        "ogg": "clerk/clerk-0a7515bb2f88f861.ogg",
        "m4a": "clerk/clerk-0a7515bb2f88f861.m4a",
        "bytes": 198023
      },
      "duration": 20.94
    },
    {
      "key": "clerk-061521b410dbf26a",
      "character": "clerk",
      "speaker": "Clerk",
      "text": "Not bad for a first day! Wait for customers until your turns run out, then see the town: Di-Mart for caskets, your office for upgrades, Spirit University if you'd like to read minds. Good luck. Try not to get stabbed.",
      "part": "whole",
      "rulesets": [
        "expanded"
      ],
      "file": {
        "ogg": "clerk/clerk-061521b410dbf26a.ogg",
        "m4a": "clerk/clerk-061521b410dbf26a.m4a",
        "bytes": 134627
      },
      "duration": 14.16
    },
    {
      "key": "clerk-545563d0787540be",
      "character": "clerk",
      "speaker": "Clerk",
      "text": "Soft Sell deals you a hand of three extras; pick one that fits under the top of the estimate. Packages upgrade the embalming, flowers, plot, headstone and service, one step at a time. Hard Sell moves them up a casket. Coffee calms someone down, once per customer. A Discount takes a little off the bill and cheers them up, twice at most. Press Done when the bill is where you want it.",
      "part": "whole",
      "rulesets": [
        "expanded"
      ],
      "file": {
        "ogg": "clerk/clerk-545563d0787540be.ogg",
        "m4a": "clerk/clerk-545563d0787540be.m4a",
        "bytes": 227980
      },
      "duration": 23.9
    },
    {
      "key": "elijah-bfceb479dcc22a4f",
      "character": "elijah",
      "speaker": "Elijah",
      "text": "Cash up front, friend. I don't do layaway on caskets. I did once. He's still in one.",
